# Opensource UI — Showcase Registry

The docs site, homepage grid, search, and `/components/[slug]` pages are driven by **`lib/showcase/showcase.tsx`**. Every showcased component must be registered here.

## Adding a new component

1. Create the file under `components/<category>/<kebab-name>.tsx`
2. Add icons to `icons/` if needed (not already in lucide-react)
3. Import at the top of `showcase.tsx`
4. Add a `c(...)` entry inside a `showcaseRows` inner array (1–3 items per row)

```tsx
import { MyNewCard } from "@/components/text/my-new-card";

c(
  "my-new-card",                              // slug → /components/my-new-card
  <MyNewCard />,                              // preview JSX
  "components/text/my-new-card.tsx",          // file path from repo root (must exist)
  "MyNewCard",                                // export name
  {
    title: "My New Card",                     // optional — defaults from slug
    description: "Shown on the detail page.",
    usage: '<MyNewCard title="Hello" />',     // optional
    isNew: true,                              // optional badge
  },
),
```

5. Update `skills/opensource-ui/references/source_inventory.txt` with the new file path
6. Verify:

```bash
npm run check:showcase   # runs on prebuild
npm run lint
npm run build
```

## Path rules

The string in `c(..., "components/...", ...)` must match the **real file on disk**. Category in the docs sidebar is derived from the folder after `components/`:

| Path | Docs category |
| ---- | ------------- |
| `components/widgets/foo.tsx` | Widgets |
| `components/buttons/foo.tsx` | Buttons |
| `components/calender/foo.tsx` | Calender |

## When moving or renaming

Update **both** in `showcase.tsx`:

1. The `import` path (`@/components/...`)
2. The `c(..., "components/.../file.tsx", ...)` string

Moving a file under `components/` does **not** auto-update the registry.

## Special preview flags

`showcase.tsx` exports helpers used by the docs preview stage:

- `isNarrowShowcaseFile` — inputs and forms
- `isFullBleedShowcaseFile` — hello loader, text loader, prism/cinder buttons
- `getShowcasePreviewBackdrop` — e.g. sheen pill button background

Add cases there when a preview needs non-default staging.
